{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791657934228,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74236ffe5avP2OYno0XijV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_00_lEJCH16OMghBrp0JkfsU6496","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"cd .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement; echo \"===ROUTING ALLOWLIST===\"; cat routing-allowlist.json; echo \"===SHARED README mentions===\"; rg -n \"agent-improvement\" scripts/shared/README.md scripts/agent-improvement/README.md references/shared/quick-reference.md | head -30; echo \"===PKG===\"; ls package.json 2>/dev/null; rg -n \"agent-improvement\" package.json 2>/dev/null"},"output":"===ROUTING ALLOWLIST===\n{\n  \"intentionally_unrouted\": [\n    {\"path\": \"assets/model-benchmark/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Lane B data-directory catalog; scripts consume the data directly, not via task intent.\"},\n    {\"path\": \"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Profile inventory catalog documenting canonical JSON configs; discovery, not live-execution guidance.\"},\n    {\"path\": \"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-fixtures/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Fixture taxonomy/inventory catalog for benchmark data; discovery aid, not a task intent.\"},\n    {\"path\": \"assets/agent-improvement/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Lane A data/config directory catalog; ownership-boundary index, not task-time material.\"},\n    {\"path\": \"assets/agent-improvement/target-profiles/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Path-consistency placeholder for dynamic-only profiles; intentional empty-directory index.\"}\n  ]\n}\n===SHARED README mentions===\nscripts/shared/README.md:16:`shared/` holds the scripts used by the deep-improvement skill's shared host surface. `loop-host.cjs` routes two modes: `agent-improvement` and `model-benchmark`. The remaining scripts are shared helpers for promotion, fixtures, state reduction, journaling, coverage tracking, argument parsing, deliverable extraction, model-family checks, fixture linting, and rubric guards.\nscripts/shared/README.md:20:- `loop-host.cjs` is the single entry point. It reads `--mode` (`agent-improvement` default, or `model-benchmark`) and spawns the resolved mode scripts.\nscripts/shared/README.md:22:- `promote-candidate.cjs` and `reduce-state.cjs` are mode-aware: they read a `mode` field on records and attribute missing or unknown modes to `agent-improvement`.\nscripts/shared/README.md:48:  Lane A names    ───▶ ../agent-improvement/<name>\nscripts/shared/README.md:79:| `loop-host.cjs` | Mode router and the only spawn host. `resolveMode()` defaults to `agent-improvement` and warns on unknown modes. `planInvocation()` builds ordered steps with BARE script names. `resolveScriptPath()` maps each bare name to its lane directory. Exports `parseArgs`, `resolveMode`, `planInvocation`, `resolveScriptPath`, `VALID_MODES`. |\nscripts/shared/README.md:82:| `reduce-state.cjs` | Reduces the runtime ledger into an experiment registry and dashboard. Buckets records by `mode` (`agent-improvement` vs `model-benchmark`), reports lane mode-mix per profile and globally, evaluates stop status, and renders journal, lineage, coverage, and mirror-sync sections. CLI: `node reduce-state.cjs <improvement-runtime-root>`. |\nscripts/shared/README.md:94:| Ownership | These scripts serve the shared deep-improvement host surface. Lane A scripts live in `../agent-improvement/` and Lane B scripts in `../model-benchmark/`. The spawn map keeps bare names in the plan and resolves the lane directory at spawn time. |\nscripts/shared/README.md:131:| `loop-host.cjs` | CLI | Mode router. `[--mode=agent-improvement] --candidate=<path>` or `--mode=model-benchmark --profile=<path-or-id> --outputs-dir=<path>`. |\nscripts/shared/README.md:149:Expected result: agent-improvement scoring runs and prints a `scored` JSON result.\nscripts/shared/README.md:163:- [`agent-improvement/README.md`](../agent-improvement/README.md)\nreferences/shared/quick-reference.md:37:The workflow copies `improvement_*` assets into the runtime, but the packet-local runtime files currently use the `agent-improvement-*` naming family shown below.\nreferences/shared/quick-reference.md:45:/deep:agent-improvement \".skilled/agents/debug.md\" :confirm --spec-folder={spec_folder}\nreferences/shared/quick-reference.md:52:node scripts/agent-improvement/scan-integration.cjs --agent=debug\nreferences/shared/quick-reference.md:55:node scripts/agent-improvement/generate-profile.cjs --agent=.skilled/agents/debug.md\nreferences/shared/quick-reference.md:58:node scripts/agent-improvement/score-candidate.cjs --candidate=.skilled/agents/debug.md\nreferences/shared/quick-reference.md:86:  agent-improvement-config.json\nreferences/shared/quick-reference.md:87:  agent-improvement-state.jsonl\nreferences/shared/quick-reference.md:88:  agent-improvement-strategy.md\nreferences/shared/quick-reference.md:89:  agent-improvement-dashboard.md\nreferences/shared/quick-reference.md:112:- `../agent-improvement/integration-scanning.md`\nscripts/agent-improvement/README.md:2:title: \"agent-improvement: Lane A Scripts\"\nscripts/agent-improvement/README.md:3:description: \"Lane A (agent-improvement) scoring, profiling, lineage, and integration scripts for the deep-improvement skill.\"\nscripts/agent-improvement/README.md:5:  - \"lane a agent-improvement scripts\"\nscripts/agent-improvement/README.md:10:# agent-improvement: Lane A Scripts\nscripts/agent-improvement/README.md:16:`agent-improvement/` holds the Lane A (agent-improvement) scripts. Lane A evaluates and improves an agent file: it builds a dynamic profile of the target agent, scores a candidate across five dimensions, scans integration surfaces, and produces lineage, drift, trade-off, and stability reporting.\nscripts/agent-improvement/README.md:20:- `score-candidate.cjs` is the lane entrypoint. `shared/loop-host.cjs` spawns it in agent-improvement mode.\nscripts/agent-improvement/README.md:31:│                      agent-improvement (Lane A)                    │\nscripts/agent-improvement/README.md:61:agent-improvement/\nscripts/agent-improvement/README.md:79:| `score-candidate.cjs` | Lane entrypoint. Reads candidate (and optional baseline), spawns `generate-profile.cjs` and `scan-integration.cjs`, scores structural, ruleCoherence, integration, outputQuality, and systemFitness dimensions, applies weights and promotion gates, caches by input hash, and emits a `scored` result with `mode: 'agent-improvement'`. |\nscripts/agent-improvement/README.md:102:│ shared/loop-host (agent-improvement mode) │\n===PKG===\n","metadata":{"output":"===ROUTING ALLOWLIST===\n{\n  \"intentionally_unrouted\": [\n    {\"path\": \"assets/model-benchmark/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Lane B data-directory catalog; scripts consume the data directly, not via task intent.\"},\n    {\"path\": \"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-profiles/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Profile inventory catalog documenting canonical JSON configs; discovery, not live-execution guidance.\"},\n    {\"path\": \"assets/model-benchmark/benchmark-fixtures/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Fixture taxonomy/inventory catalog for benchmark data; discovery aid, not a task intent.\"},\n    {\"path\": \"assets/agent-improvement/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Lane A data/config directory catalog; ownership-boundary index, not task-time material.\"},\n    {\"path\": \"assets/agent-improvement/target-profiles/README.md\", \"reason\": \"Path-consistency placeholder for dynamic-only profiles; intentional empty-directory index.\"}\n  ]\n}\n===SHARED README mentions===\nscripts/shared/README.md:16:`shared/` holds the scripts used by the deep-improvement skill's shared host surface. `loop-host.cjs` routes two modes: `agent-improvement` and `model-benchmark`. The remaining scripts are shared helpers for promotion, fixtures, state reduction, journaling, coverage tracking, argument parsing, deliverable extraction, model-family checks, fixture linting, and rubric guards.\nscripts/shared/README.md:20:- `loop-ho