{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791658342064,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74236ffe5avP2OYno0XijV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"bash","callID":"call_01_rXe4KuaSV40QMpNLPKt21605","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"command":"rg -n \"agent-improvement|deep-improvement\" .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/SKILL.md .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/assets/prompt-templates.md .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/references/agent-delegation.md .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/references/cli-reference.md .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/README.md .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/references/agent-delegation.md .skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/references/claude-tools.md .skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-opencode/assets/checklists/agent-authoring.md 2>/dev/null | head -40"},"output":".skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/references/agent-delegation.md:102:├── deep-improvement.md # Proposal-only agent-improvement candidates (command-owned)\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/references/agent-delegation.md:132:| `deep-improvement` | default | Proposal-only agent-improvement candidate generation | Command-owned by `/deep:agent-improvement` — never dispatch directly |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-opencode/assets/checklists/agent-authoring.md:37:- [ ] Read the mirror checker at `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs`; it treats `.skilled/agents/` as canonical and `.claude/agents/` as the runtime mirror.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-opencode/assets/checklists/agent-authoring.md:65:- [ ] Mirror parity check: run `node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs --all` after editing agent mirrors.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-opencode/assets/checklists/agent-authoring.md:73:- Mirror checker: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs`\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/README.md:57:| **deep-improvement** | proposal-only deep-improvement candidate generation, command-owned |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/references/claude-tools.md:247:| **Agent System** | 12 agents via `.claude/agents/*.md`, all directly invokable with `--agent <name>` | 12 agents via `.skilled/agents/*.md`, split into 3 classes: primary (`general`, `plan`, `orchestrate` — only `orchestrate` is a project file usable with top-level `--agent`), subagent (`context`, `markdown`, `review`, `debug`, `ai-council` — routed via `--agent orchestrate`, never direct), and command-owned (`deep-research`, `deep-review`, `deep-improvement`, `prompt-improver` — dispatched only by their parent `/deep:*` command) |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/references/agent-delegation.md:80:`--agent <slug>` is valid at the top level ONLY for the primary agent `orchestrate` (and `plan`, an OpenCode built-in) — never for `general` (rejected, omit `--agent` instead) and never for a subagent slug (`context`, `markdown`, `review`, `debug`, `ai-council`) or a command-owned loop executor (`deep-research`, `deep-review`, `deep-improvement`, `prompt-improver`), all of which route through `--agent orchestrate`'s Task-dispatch or their owning `/deep:*` command (§3-4 below). When `--agent orchestrate` IS used, the flag loads the agent definition from `.opencode/agents/orchestrate.md` (project-local) or the user-level fallback. The dispatch shape pins model, variant, format, and working directory alongside the agent slug:\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/references/agent-delegation.md:134:| `deep-improvement` | Command-owned by `/deep:agent-improvement`; never direct `--agent deep-improvement` | Proposal-only mutator for bounded agent improvement | Agent evaluation via the `/deep:agent-improvement` command loop |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/references/agent-delegation.md:231:| Agent improvement | `deep-improvement` | **Command-only.** Dispatch via `/deep:agent-improvement`. Direct `opencode run --agent deep-improvement` is forbidden; the parent command owns evaluation, candidates, and promotion. |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/assets/prompt-templates.md:188:- **Command-owned loop executors (never direct `--agent`)**: `deep-research` (via `/deep:research`), `deep-review` (via `/deep:review`), `deep-improvement` (via `/deep:agent-improvement`), `prompt-improver` (via `/prompt`'s deep-path escalation).\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/references/cli-reference.md:294:| `deep-improvement` | Agent improvement proposal mutator |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/SKILL.md:30:- **Agent dispatch** — task matches a specialized OpenCode agent. Primary agents (directly invokable via `--agent`): `general`, `plan` (built-in), `orchestrate`. Generic subagents fully dispatched via the orchestrate primary: `context`, `review`, `write`, `debug`, `ai-council`. Command-owned loop executors (`deep-research`, `deep-review`, `deep-improvement`, `prompt-improver`) are owned end-to-end by their parent `/deep:*` command; `orchestrate` may perform exactly one bounded hand-off dispatch to a recognized loop request, but never manages the loop itself. See §3 \"OpenCode Agent Delegation\" for the full contract.\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-opencode/SKILL.md:197:3. **Command-owned loop executors** (`deep-research`, `deep-review`, `deep-improvement`, `prompt-improver`) — LOOP-OWNED by their parent commands (`/deep:research`, `/deep:review`, `/deep:agent-improvement`, `/prompt`), which own iteration state, convergence detection, and continuity. Never dispatch these directly via raw `--agent <slug>`. `orchestrate` is an authorized **caller/coordinator only** — it may perform exactly one bounded hand-off dispatch to the resolved leaf, but MUST NOT re-implement the loop.\n","metadata":{"output":".skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/references/agent-delegation.md:102:├── deep-improvement.md # Proposal-only agent-improvement candidates (command-owned)\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/references/agent-delegation.md:132:| `deep-improvement` | default | Proposal-only agent-improvement candidate generation | Command-owned by `/deep:agent-improvement` — never dispatch directly |\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-opencode/assets/checklists/agent-authoring.md:37:- [ ] Read the mirror checker at `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs`; it treats `.skilled/agents/` as canonical and `.claude/agents/` as the runtime mirror.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-opencode/assets/checklists/agent-authoring.md:65:- [ ] Mirror parity check: run `node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs --all` after editing agent mirrors.\n.skilled/skills/sk-code/sk-code-opencode/assets/checklists/agent-authoring.md:73:- Mirror checker: `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs`\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/README.md:57:| **deep-improvement** | proposal-only deep-improvement candidate generation, command-owned |\n.skilled/skills/cli-external-orchestration/cli-claude-code/references/claude-tools.md:247:| **Agent System** | 12 agents via `.claude/agents/*.md`, all directly invokable with `--agent <name>` | 12 agents via `.skilled/agents/*.md`, split into 3 classes: primary (`general`, `plan`, `orchestrate` — only `orchestrate` is a project file usable with top-level `--agent`), subagent (`context`, `markdown`, `review`, `debug`, `ai-council` — routed via `--agent orchestrate`, never direct), and command-owned (`deep-research`, `deep-review`