mirror-sync-verify.cjs']) {\n./.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/tests/check-agent-mirror-sync.vitest.ts:62:describe('check-agent-mirror-sync', () => {\n./.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/tests/README.md:45:    +-- check-agent-mirror-sync.vitest.ts  # covers check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs\n./.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/shared/tests/README.md:86:| `check-agent-mirror-sync.vitest.ts` | `check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs` agent path matching and its drift exit, run from a fixture copy. |\n./.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs:3:// ║ check-agent-mirror-sync — block agent edits that desync runtime mirrors  ║\n./.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/README.md:79:An agent is more than its `.md` file. `scan-integration.cjs` inventories the canonical agent definition (`.skilled/agents/`), its Claude runtime mirror (`.claude/agents/`), command dispatch files, YAML workflow assets, skill references and the skill-advisor routing path. The scanner extracts emphasized strings from the canonical agent and marks a mirror aligned when enough of them appear. A drifted mirror shows up before it causes a runtime surprise, and the score reflects the whole integration surface, not the prompt in isolation. Mirror parity is also enforced repo-wide outside a scoring run: `scripts/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs` gates commits (through `.skilled/hooks/git/pre-commit`) and pull requests into `main` (through `.github/workflows/agent-mirror-sync.yml`), so drifted runtime copies are caught before they merge. The commit hook fails open when Node or the checker is unavailable so it never blocks an unrelated commit; the CI gate on `main` is the fail-closed backstop.\n./.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/references/shared/agent-mirror-crosswalk.md:52:- `node .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs --all`\n./.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/changelog/v1.17.0.0.md:21:- **The mirror check now runs on every commit and pull request.** Every agent is authored once under `.opencode/agents/<name>.md` as the canonical body and mirrored to `.claude/agents/<name>.md` and `.codex/agents/<name>.toml`. A new `scripts/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs` wraps the existing `verifyMirrorSync` library as a gate over the changed agent files, or over every agent with `--all`. It fails when an agent's mirrors drift from the canonical body, including a deleted mirror or a deleted canonical whose runtime copies still linger. `.opencode/hooks/git/pre-commit` runs it over added, modified and deleted agent paths, and a new `.github/workflows/agent-mirror-sync.yml` runs it on pull requests and fails closed if the checker is ever removed. The deep-improvement README surfaces the gate in its Integration Scan section.\n./.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/changelog/v1.17.0.0.md:27:No migration required. The gate is additive. It runs against changed agent files at commit time and against the full set in CI, and it only fails when a mirror genuinely diverges from its `.opencode` canonical. Run `node .opencode/skills/deep-loop-workflows/deep-improvement/scripts/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs --all` to verify all mirrors locally.\n./.skilled/scripts/git-hooks/pre-commit:165:MIRROR_CHECKER=\"$SOURCE_ROOT/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs\"\n===LOOP-HOST OUTSIDE===\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/feature-catalog/deep-loop-mode-classification/deep-loop-mode-classification.md:28:Every packet carries `workflowMode` (the public mode key: `research`, `review`, `ai-council`, and the two improvement lanes `agent-improvement`, `model-benchmark`), `runtimeLoopType` (the graph-backed convergence key consumed by `runtime/scripts/convergence.cjs`, validated against active `research`/`review`/`council`, and explicitly `null` for both improvement lanes rather than inferred from `workflowMode` — `ai-council` maps to `runtimeLoopType: council`), and `backendKind` (`runtime-loop-type` for research/review/ai-council, `improvement-host` for the two improvement lanes, run via `deep-improvement/scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode`).\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:62:- **`backendKind`** — which backend runs the mode: `runtime-loop-type` (research/review/ai-council) or `improvement-host` (`deep-improvement/scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode`).\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md:84:     else: backend = improvement loop-host (--mode), per backendKind\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/mode-registry.json:9:    \"backendKind\": \"Which backend actually runs the mode: runtime-loop-type (runtime/ convergence) or improvement-host (deep-improvement/scripts/shared/loop-host.cjs --mode).\"\n.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/benchmark/reports/compiled-routing/2026-07-21--real--luna-high/skill-benchmark-report.json:29:        \"stderr\": \"OpenAI Codex v0.144.4\\n--------\\nworkdir: /Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/.worktrees/0089-sk-doc-default-routing-cutover\\nmodel: gpt-5.6-luna\\nprovider: openai\\napproval: never\\nsandbox: read-only\\nreasoning effort: high\\nreasoning summaries: none\\nsession id: 019f83a2-2f88-7d92-a701-956e20c79296\\n--------\\nuser\\nYou are analyzing skill routing only - do NOT edit files.\\nTask: Use deep research to investigate why our advisor sometimes routes iterative investigation prompts incorrectly, and write the findings as a research summary.\\n\\nWithin the `system-deep-loop` skill ONLY (do not route to or read any other skill), consulting that skill's SKILL.md router, determine: (1) the detected SURFACE if the skill defines one (e.g. WEBFLOW / OPENCODE), else \\\"UNKNOWN\\\", (2) the sub-language if any, else \\\"none\\\", (3) the exact reference/asset file paths you would load (relative to the skill root, e.g. references/... and asset