{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1791658732396,"sessionID":"ses_ed8e74236ffe5avP2OYno0XijV","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"write","callID":"call_00_hKiDmiRegRNwX1Cc7dYi1114","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"content":"# Iteration 7: Runtime mirrors B — `.codex/` copies, `.pi/` copies, symlink chains, Hermes generated skill mirrors\n\n## Focus\n\nClassify every agent-improvement surface in `.codex/`, `.cursor/`, `.pi/`, `.devin/` and `.hermes/` as symlink, generated copy or hand-written file, including the Hermes `agent-*` skill mirrors and prompt stubs, and establish the regeneration path for each generated artifact.\n\n## Actions Taken\n\n1. `ls -la` on `.codex/`, `.cursor/`, `.pi/`, `.devin/`, `.hermes/` roots and their `agents/` directories.\n2. `rg -l` for the mode tokens across the five trees, then per-file inspection of the matches (`.codex/agents`, `.codex/prompts`, `.pi/agents`, `.pi/prompts`, `.hermes/skills`, `.hermes/prompts`).\n3. Read the `.hermes` generated-file headers and `.hermes/SYNC.md` mirror contract; verified the generator scripts under `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/hermes/`.\n4. Read `check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs` header and path regex to determine the checker's agent-path coverage.\n\n## Findings\n\n1. **`.codex/agents/deep-improvement.toml` is a real generated TOML copy** (15,807 bytes) in a directory of per-agent `.toml` files; it sits inside the mirror checker's coverage (`AGENT_PATH_RE` includes `.codex/agents/`). Disposition: DELETE (regenerate after the canonical agent goes). [SOURCE: .codex/agents/deep-improvement.toml]\n2. **`.codex/prompts/deep-agent-improvement.md` is a real prompt copy** alongside 38 sibling prompt files. Disposition: DELETE. [SOURCE: .codex/prompts/deep-agent-improvement.md]\n3. **`.cursor/agents/deep-improvement.md` is a symlink to `../../.claude/agents/deep-improvement.md`** — it dies when the `.claude` copy is deleted; no separate edit. [SOURCE: .cursor/agents/deep-improvement.md]\n4. **`.devin/agents/deep-improvement/AGENT.md` is a symlink to `../../../.claude/agents/deep-improvement.md`** — same symlink chain as Cursor; no separate edit. [SOURCE: .devin/agents/deep-improvement/AGENT.md]\n5. **`.pi/agents/deep-improvement.md` is a real hand-synced copy** (15,741 bytes) that the agent-mirror checker does NOT cover: `check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs` path regex accepts only `.opencode|.skilled|.claude|.codex/agents/`, so `.pi`, `.devin` and `.hermes` agent copies live outside the drift gate. Disposition: DELETE. [SOURCE: .pi/agents/deep-improvement.md]\n6. **`.pi/prompts/deep-agent-improvement.md` is a real prompt copy.** Disposition: DELETE. [SOURCE: .pi/prompts/deep-agent-improvement.md]\n7. **`.hermes/agents` is a whole-directory symlink to `../.skilled/agents`** — Hermes reads the canonical agent files; no Hermes agent copy to edit. [SOURCE: .hermes/agents]\n8. **`.hermes/skills/agent-deep-improvement/SKILL.md` is a generated preloadable agent-skill mirror** — header: \"generated by sync-skills-hermes.cjs; do not edit\", persona from the shared agent files. Disposition: DELETE via regeneration (write mode prunes stale folders). [SOURCE: .hermes/skills/agent-deep-improvement/SKILL.md:6]\n9. **`.hermes/skills/deep-improvement/SKILL.md` is the generated Hermes copy of the packet SKILL.md** (full frontmatter with the packet's triggers incl. `model-benchmark mode`). Disposition: EDIT via regeneration (the shared packet survives for Lane B; the copy tracks its canonical). [SOURCE: .hermes/skills/deep-improvement/SKILL.md]\n10. **Four further Hermes skill copies carry the mode through their canonicals** — `.hermes/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md`, `cli-opencode/SKILL.md`, `cli-devin/SKILL.md`, `cli-cursor/SKILL.md`, `sk-create-benchmark/SKILL.md`. Disposition: EDIT via regeneration after the canonical docs in iterations 1/4/5 are edited. [SOURCE: .hermes/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md]\n11. **`.hermes/prompts/deep-agent-improvement.md` is a generated pointer stub** — header names `sync-prompts-hermes.cjs` and the canonical `.skilled/commands/deep/agent-improvement.md`. Disposition: DELETE via regeneration. [SOURCE: .hermes/prompts/deep-agent-improvement.md:1]\n12. **The Hermes generators and their check modes are the regeneration path** — `.hermes/SYNC.md` lines 24-25 document `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` and `prompts/*.md` as generated, lines 50-51 require re-running `sync-skills-hermes.cjs` / `sync-prompts-hermes.cjs` after canonical changes, line 63 shows the `--check` mode; both scripts exist under `.skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/hermes/`. Disposition: run after canonical edits (no direct file edits). [SOURCE: .hermes/SYNC.md:63]\n13. **Mirror taxonomy for the mode across runtimes is now complete** — canonical `.skilled/agents/deep-improvement.md`; translated physical copies in `.claude` (governed by the checker) and `.codex` (TOML, governed), symlink chains in `.cursor`/`.devin` (via `.claude`), hand copies in `.pi` (ungoverned), generated copies in `.hermes` (via sync scripts), and symlink farm in `.opencode`. [SOURCE: .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs:33]\n\n## Ruled Out\n\n- Expecting `.cursor`, `.devin` or `.hermes` to hold independent agent bodies: each resolves through a symlink or a generator to a canonical file already inventoried.\n\n## Dead Ends\n\n- None; the five trees resolved into three chains (symlink to `.claude`, hand copy in `.pi`, generated in `.hermes`).\n\n## Edge Cases\n\n- Ambiguous input: whether generated Hermes files count as \"references\" for the inventory — resolved by listing them as generated mirrors with their regeneration entry point.\n- Contradictory evidence: none.\n- Missing dependencies: none.\n- Partial success: none.\n\n## Sources Consulted\n\n- .codex/agents/deep-improvement.toml; .codex/prompts/deep-agent-improvement.md\n- .cursor/agents/deep-improvement.md (symlink)\n- .devin/agents/deep-improvement/AGENT.md (symlink)\n- .pi/agents/deep-improvement.md; .pi/prompts/deep-agent-improvement.md\n- .hermes/agents (symlink); .hermes/skills/agent-deep-improvement/SKILL.md:6; .hermes/skills/deep-improvement/SKILL.md; .hermes/skills/system-deep-loop/SKILL.md; .hermes/prompts/deep-agent-improvement.md:1\n- .hermes/SYNC.md:24-25,50-51,63\n- .skilled/skills/system-spec-kit/runtime/cli/hermes/ (sync-skills-hermes.cjs, sync-prompts-hermes.cjs)\n- .skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/deep-improvement/scripts/check-agent-mirror-sync.cjs:8-35\n\n## Assessment\n\n- New information ratio: 0.9\n- Questions addressed: KQ3 (mirror nature across all seven runtime dirs — completed), KQ1 (mirror-side references)\n- Questions answered: the runtime-mirror nature question is now answered in full across `.claude .opencode .codex .cursor .pi .devin .hermes`\n\n## Reflection\n\n- What worked and why: per-directory `ls -la` distinguishes symlinks, hand copies and generated copies in one pass; the generated-file headers then named their generators exactly.\n- What did not work and why: nothing failed; the checker regex reading added the coverage-gap nuance (`.pi` ungoverned).\n- What I would do differently: in synthesis, present the mirror taxonomy as one table keyed by runtime so the deletion plan can sequence symlink-first removals.\n\n## SCOPE VIOLATIONS\n\n- None.\n\n## Recommended Next Focus\n\nIteration 8: history and documentation surfaces — the hub packet's own benchmark reports, changelog trees, feature-catalog, manual-testing-playbook, behavior-benchmark scenarios, the root README.md and `.skilled/README`, plus the `.skilled/skills/system-deep-loop/changelog` and root changelog live-vs-history boundary.\n","filePath":"/Users/michelkerkmeester/MEGA/Development/Code_Environment/Public/specs/system-deep-loop/039-deprecate-improvement-modes/001-removal-research/002-agent-improvement-inventory/research/lineages/deepseek/iterations/iteration-007.md"},"output":"Wrote file successfully.","metadata":{"diagnostics